-- title:
--   Avg Over Avg Over Phase Two Linear
-- statement:
--   **Linearity for two nested distribution averages in a bipartite expectation.**
--
--   Let $\mathcal D_Q$ and $\mathcal D_V$ be finite-support weighted distributions, let $\Gamma$ and $A$ be finite outcome types, let $\psi$ be a bipartite state, and let $F$, $P$, and $R$ be the operator families in the statement. No probability assumption is required. Finite linearity gives
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb{E}_{v\sim\mathcal D_V}\mathbb{E}_{q\sim\mathcal D_Q}\left[\sum_{g,a}\operatorname{ev}_\psi\left((F(q,g,a)R)\otimes P(g,v)\right)\right]=\sum_g\operatorname{ev}_\psi\left(\left(\mathbb{E}_{q\sim\mathcal D_Q}\sum_aF(q,g,a)\right)R\otimes\mathbb{E}_{v\sim\mathcal D_V}P(g,v)\right).
--   $$
--
--   The two operator averages are the formal `averageOperatorOverDistribution` terms. This is the linear algebra step used by the phase-two question-defect reduction.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.avgOver_avgOver_phaseTwo_linear`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Commutativity/ScalarApproximation/ProcessedG/PhaseTwo.lean#L142-L230

